35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,It seems our internal capacity to manage a transition is much lower than we've officially acknowledged.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I knew it! Our yard gear is a mess and we can't afford a blackout during the peak season.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The financial patterns are concerning. We are paying more for the pieces we didn't buy outright.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Oh dear! It looks like we really struggle with who is in charge when things break. We can't let that happen again!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,How predictable. We have a habit of letting systems age into obsolescence and paying consultants to leave us with puzzles.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if we don't have the people to support it, the ""ownership"" of the vendor won't matter. The staff will just burn out.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I get the cost thing, but if the system doesn't work on the floor, it's a waste of money anyway!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, a system that works but bankrupts us through hidden renewal fees is also a failure.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"Let's try to find a way to make everyone happy! We just need a vendor who is really, really clear about their support!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests we avoid any vendor that encourages ""black box"" implementations or requires excessive external hand-holding for basic updates.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"We need a vendor that provides extensive, hands-on training and doesn't assume we have a full IT team.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And they have to be okay with old hardware! I won't support a vendor that forces us to buy 500 new tablets overnight.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I will be looking for a vendor with a transparent, flat-fee structure for renewals. No hidden escalations.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll be cheering for the one that gives us a clear map of who to call at 3 AM!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall be looking for the one that prioritizes modularity and clean data migration over flashy, monolithic promises.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
