60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I prefer Anchor. Having their engineers on-site during the rollout is the only way to ensure our stretched staff aren't overwhelmed.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Anchor sounds great too! If they are on-site, they can actually see the old yard devices and make sure the software works with them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Corvus is a nightmare. Separate licenses for every component mean separate renewal hikes. I cannot support a fragmented billing model.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I'm worried about Corvus too! If it's all separate, who do we call when the whole thing breaks? Meridian sounds much more organized!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Corvus is indeed a recipe for a fragmented mess. However, Tessera's reliance on a ""partner firm"" for migration is a red flag.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, Meridian's ""fixed configuration"" sounds like it will ignore the reality of how our depot supervisors actually work.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! ""Fixed"" means it won't bend to our peak-season chaos. Anchor's on-site team can adapt to the floor.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Meridian's hosted suite with a fixed configuration usually implies a more predictable cost structure. It avoids the ""death by a thousand cuts"" of add-ons.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if it's too fixed, it might stop matching our business in a few months! I want something that can grow with us!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Meridian is the safest bet for those who fear chaos, but Anchor is the only one that addresses the ""aging in place"" risk by ensuring a proper hand-off.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm sticking with Anchor. We can't afford a failure that leaves our few remaining administrators to clean up the mess alone.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki. Anchor is the only one that feels like they'll actually step into the yard and solve the problem.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I find Anchor's on-premise model risky for long-term costs, but Meridian's hosted suite is the most fiscally transparent option here.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I want to be helpful! If Misaki and Kenji really need Anchor to keep the depots running, I'll support them!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I appreciate the sentiment, I must prioritize the technical integrity of the migration. Anchor's on-site presence reduces the risk of ""repair work"" later.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
76,3,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for Meridian. The risk of escalating costs in other models is too high to ignore.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
